# Shell scripts run on Linux runners and are parsed by `bash -n` in
# tests/test_deploy_scripts.py. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout
# turned them CRLF and those tests failed here for that reason alone.
# They are LF everywhere, always.
*.sh text eol=lf

# JSONL forward-capture stores (src/pipeline/store_archive.py, 2026-09-21
# archive-rotation incident) must be byte-for-byte identical to what the
# writer produced -- `rotate`'s own verification proof depends on it, and
# so does every reader that hashes or diffs raw lines. src.pipeline.
# snapshots.append writes them LF-only. Without this, a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true (this machine, 2026-09-21 review: a 319,571-byte
# gap between this checkout's odds_multibook.jsonl and its HEAD blob, one
# CR per line) silently turns every line CRLF on checkout, which would
# break that proof for anyone running a local capture loop on Windows --
# store_archive.py's own module docstring explicitly supports that case
# ("Windows dev boxes included").
data/processed/*.jsonl text eol=lf
